meta {
  name: Reconcile payments (PLANNED - not implemented)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{internal_base}}/internal/reconcile
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{service_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "provider": "TRON_TRC20",
    "sinceMinutes": 60
  }
}

docs {
  ⚠️ THIS ENDPOINT DOES NOT EXIST YET — sending this request returns 404.

  It is kept as the agreed shape for an on-demand reconciliation trigger, as
  described in docs/AGENT_PLAN.md. Today reconciliation runs ONLY as the
  worker's scheduled `payments:poll` job, which re-checks CryptoBot invoices
  for orders still PENDING; there is no HTTP entry point to force a pass.

  To implement: add the route under apps/bot/src/server/routes/internal/,
  behind the existing SERVICE_TOKEN guard, and have it enqueue the worker's
  reconciliation job rather than doing the work in the request.
}
